[{"n":1,"title":"Rushup Edge","artist":"The Tuss","year":2007,"mbid":"8af1251f-ce01-3baf-b960-93c00e7baf45","heard":false,"cover":"https://dn710301.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-e1d2128c-436a-4584-95f5-07da18f3fba0/mbid-e1d2128c-436a-4584-95f5-07da18f3fba0-2573352078.jpg","spotify_id":null,"spotify_url":null,"desc_lfm_album":"Rushup Edge is the first studio album released by electronic artist, The Tuss on June 25, 2007, released under Rephlex Records. The name of the album is an immediate reference to a mountain ridge in the British county of Derbyshire, the namesake of the album, Rushup Edge. It is speculated that Richard D. James, primarily known under the pseudonym/stage name of Aphex Twin is the true creator of this album, although it is unproven. The album is credited to the known members of The Tuss, Karen and Brian Tregaskin. Oddly enough the album Rushup Edge is available for purchase on .","desc_lfm_artist":"The Tuss is an electronic music project by Richard D. James of Aphex Twin fame. Before the official reveal of Richard D. James as being The Tuss, it was originally theorized that The Tuss was a group consisting of Cornish musicians Brian Tregaskin and Karen Tregaskin. So far The Tuss's releases are an EP, \"Confederation Trough\" and an album, \"Rushup Edge\". Both have been released on Rephlex in 2007. \n\nIn July 2017,  seven new tracks were added to \"Rushup Edge\", and can be found here : https://aphextwin.","desc_mb_album":null,"desc_mb_artist":null,"yt_id":"R-5koLtMy98","genres":["electro","idm","techno","acid techno"],"rym":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/the-tuss/rushup-edge","scaruffi_rating":null,"scaruffi_note":null,"wikipedia_url":null,"aoty_user_score":null,"aoty_critic_score":null,"metacritic_score":null,"label":null},{"n":2,"title":"The Seventh Dream","artist":"Dream Dolphin","year":1997,"mbid":"49b1915f-21da-4ed8-9549-9095a30e5d48","heard":false,"cover":"https://coverartarchive.org/release-group/49b1915f-21da-4ed8-9549-9095a30e5d4